{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c01b059ad887781a","type":"text","text":"Arp Ping Scan","x":-138,"y":-202,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d9d0c98dd997c684","type":"text","text":"`Address Resolution Protocol`","x":160,"y":-202,"width":260,"height":60},
		{"id":"d01f15c4a3844790","type":"text","text":"```\nIP address ko MAC address me convert karna\n```","x":520,"y":-243,"width":250,"height":142},
		{"id":"fe2f506d67c438c2","type":"text","text":"Local network mai data share karane ke liye mac address chahiye hota hai","x":860,"y":-223,"width":250,"height":103},
		{"id":"b2f35a0aad57642d","type":"text","text":"Live hosts discover karna\nRouter\nLaptop 1\nLaptop 2\nMobile\nPrinter","x":1400,"y":-262,"width":250,"height":181},
		{"id":"e17afc229998f6a7","type":"text","text":"ICMP block hone par bhi kaam karta hai\nLekin local `LAN` me `arp allowed` hai","x":1374,"y":-429,"width":366,"height":69},
		{"id":"4dbd79127a82bbad","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PR 10.66.104.227`","x":1920,"y":-292,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"11a12c82c7210834","type":"text","text":"-sn : Disable port scanning only host discovery\n-PR : arp ping scan","x":2295,"y":-293,"width":385,"height":60},
		{"id":"43f9b80d64405128","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/arp_ping_scan.png","x":2820,"y":-314,"width":400,"height":102},
		{"id":"7df30e947610ff76","type":"text","text":"TCP SYN ping","x":270,"y":280,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"046f30273e475d67","type":"text","text":"TCP ACK ping","x":270,"y":397,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f132cbcd543dde67","type":"text","text":"Tcp ping scan","x":-122,"y":397,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c4cec53fd22d2b03","type":"text","text":"Udp Ping Scan","x":-138,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2323dfed0abe0771","type":"text","text":"**UDP Ping Scan** ka use ye check karne ke liye hota hai ki **koi host (device) alive hai ya nahi** by sending **UDP packets**.","x":-138,"y":80,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"8d015e67f65ff55a","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PU 10.66.104.227`","x":160,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"80096182bd1f09e8","type":"text","text":"Default port scan : 40125","x":520,"y":-80,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"99f1bb7c7854e7ba","type":"text","text":"Jab ICMP block ho ya UDP services test karni ho","x":520,"y":20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"672464e053245bd2","type":"text","text":"Same LAN/Wi-Fi","x":-138,"y":-293,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"4bdd9e271d710043","type":"text","text":"`TCP SYN Ping` ek host discovery method hai jisme Nmap `TCP SYN packet` bhejta hai. Agar target `SYN-ACK` ya `RST` reply karta hai to pata chalta hai ki host `alive` hai. Iska use tab karte hain jab ICMP ping `firewall ki wajah se block ho` ya network me `live hosts discover` karne ho.","x":580,"y":250,"width":574,"height":120},
		{"id":"eb83cb3e4ce1df13","type":"text","text":"`PS22-25, PS80, 113, 1050, 3500`","x":1240,"y":280,"width":280,"height":60},
		{"id":"63a82719cbe199d9","type":"text","text":"TCP SYN ping can be used to determine if the host is active without creating any connection . `logs are not recorded` at system or `network level` ","x":1240,"y":80,"width":280,"height":153},
		{"id":"fdbaf34721d08c66","type":"text","text":"TCP ACK ping also uses the default port 80. `send -> TCP ACK empty flag to the target.` \nNo connection : Receiving ACK packet. \nTarget Host Respond : RST flag to terminate\n\t","x":580,"y":397,"width":574,"height":120},
		{"id":"8dfe86a5fc21c561","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PA 10.34.104.34`","x":1330,"y":427,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6111c568c1aa397a","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PP 10.32.23.2`","x":1179,"y":1175,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ec95a74fff4c13b1","type":"text","text":"Specially When the administrator blocks the traditional ICMP echo ping ","x":1179,"y":1255,"width":250,"height":78},
		{"id":"c5a5dcd3f0df519a","type":"text","text":"`-PM` option used to perform ICMP address mask ping scan","x":1527,"y":1255,"width":273,"height":78},
		{"id":"8a3ab2fd6a23a09f","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PM 10.34.104.45`","x":1896,"y":1265,"width":248,"height":60},
		{"id":"2adbff8012062408","type":"text","text":"- Scanner ek IP range choose karta hai.\n- Har IP address par ICMP Echo Request bhejta hai.\n- Agar host active hai aur ICMP allow karta hai to:\n    - **ICMP Echo Reply (Type 0)** return karta hai.\n- Reply milne par host ko **alive/up** maana jata hai.","x":1480,"y":1007,"width":439,"height":166},
		{"id":"924ab335f1905893","type":"text","text":"`-PE` ICMP ping echo scan","x":2020,"y":1060,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7a73e95837ce4d43","type":"text","text":"For Ping sweep that will be used of ip range","x":2456,"y":1058,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"379df08a154a3bd6","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PE 10.10.23.23-24`","x":2796,"y":1058,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ab590064c3181e20","type":"text","text":"```\n-P : ICMP scan\n-L : increase the number of ping\n-T : Timestamp\n-E : echo\n-PE: ICMP ECHO ping scan\n-sn: disable port scanning\n```","x":440,"y":821,"width":358,"height":205},
		{"id":"07164b973b5ebf63","type":"text","text":"ICMP echo ping sweep","x":602,"y":1060,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"74ba2fa920414eb8","type":"text","text":"Timestamp message acquire the info ralated to the current time from the target host machine. ","x":621,"y":1174,"width":399,"height":60},
		{"id":"aa6b77576f15db6f","type":"text","text":"The attacker send an ICMP address mask qry to the target host to acquire information related to the subnet mask.","x":623,"y":1247,"width":395,"height":95},
		{"id":"892685de6c46c500","type":"text","text":"**ICMP Echo Request (Type 8)** packets bhej kar check kiya jata hai ki network me kaun-kaun se hosts active hain.","x":952,"y":1040,"width":378,"height":100},
		{"id":"14550ec42aee9641","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PE 10.24.104.227`","x":1080,"y":894,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0c1902902a1de80d","type":"text","text":"ICMP echo ping scan","x":266,"y":1060,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"914584f2aba4bcfa","type":"text","text":"ICMP echo time stamp ping","x":270,"y":1174,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"efa4ebc65d8f9214","type":"text","text":"ICMP Address mask ping","x":270,"y":1264,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d22e9fa22d6c5577","type":"text","text":"ICMP ping scan","x":-112,"y":1174,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4c48b94346a85323","type":"text","text":"ICMP ping scan  port abstraction ko include nahi karata h or ye port scanning se bahut alag h ","x":-140,"y":960,"width":360,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6f842214a42e5f78","type":"text","text":"Ip Protocol scan","x":-140,"y":620,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"577b515556826db6","type":"text","text":"This technique try to send diffrent packets using diffrent IP protocols","x":220,"y":610,"width":296,"height":80},
		{"id":"316a2f1c691a775d","type":"text","text":"Multiple ip packets for \nICMP -> Protocol 1\nIGMP -> Protocol 2\nIP-IN-IP -> Protocol 4\nthese are sent by default.","x":602,"y":572,"width":250,"height":157},
		{"id":"88a6fea567c591f9","type":"text","text":"**IP Protocol Ping Scan** ek **host discovery technique** hai jisme ICMP ya TCP/UDP ports ki jagah **different IP protocol numbers** wale packets bheje jaate hain taaki pata chale ki host alive hai ya nahi.","x":958,"y":581,"width":372,"height":139},
		{"id":"13dbff4296d3ae6a","type":"text","text":"| Protocol Number | Protocol |\n| --------------: | -------- |\n|               1 | ICMP     |\n|               2 | IGMP     |\n|               6 | TCP      |\n|              17 | UDP      |\n|              47 | GRE      |\n|              50 | ESP      |\n|              51 | AH       |","x":1919,"y":487,"width":274,"height":276},
		{"id":"b0baee2aaab5e3b0","type":"text","text":"IP Protocol Ping Scan is a host discovery technique in which Nmap sends raw IP packets with specific protocol numbers instead of ICMP or TCP. If the target responds (for example, with an ICMP Protocol Unreachable message or another protocol-specific response), the host is considered alive.","x":2340,"y":559,"width":604,"height":133},
		{"id":"fc87297a6636ca17","type":"text","text":"# Host Discovery","x":-960,"y":397,"width":211,"height":60},
		{"id":"eddee1ca3a98fdc8","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/udp-ping-scan.png","x":910,"y":-50,"width":400,"height":98},
		{"id":"b618e24a1fd04cb1","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PS 10.10.23.2`","x":1655,"y":119,"width":250,"height":75},
		{"id":"f1a22289166644ce","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/tcp_syn_ping_scan.png","x":2040,"y":109,"width":400,"height":95},
		{"id":"c2b6d2ebf313bd71","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/tcp_ping_ack_scan.png","x":1719,"y":360,"width":400,"height":97},
		{"id":"50425953f1dc54f9","type":"text","text":"Advantage: \nBoth `SYN` and `ACK` can be used to bypass firewall","x":1719,"y":250,"width":408,"height":60},
		{"id":"666a6be4b48c5e16","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PO1,2,4 10.66.104.34`","x":1503,"y":733,"width":276,"height":60},
		{"id":"7e4476c129dd3696","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sn -PO 192.168.1.10`","x":1503,"y":529,"width":277,"height":60},
		{"id":"9e262f764ec39569","type":"text","text":"- `-sn` → Sirf host discovery, port scan nahi.\n- `-PO` → IP Protocol Ping.\n- `1,2,4` → Ye protocol numbers hain:\n    - `1` = ICMP\n    - `2` = IGMP\n    - `4` = IP-in-IP","x":1919,"y":793,"width":382,"height":191},
		{"id":"0bf0d87757f0d555","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/ip_protocol_scan.png","x":2420,"y":842,"width":400,"height":93},
		{"id":"261b4fb12d33d792","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/icmp_ping_echo_scan.png","x":1379,"y":907,"width":400,"height":95},
		{"id":"d6a6af82d78fd15a","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/ping_mask.png","x":2240,"y":1265,"width":399,"height":59}
	],
